    "directions": [
      "Soak tadka'r daal (green moong beans) and chhola'r daal (split Bengal gram) overnight. The next morning, drain them over a colander.",
      "Make a spice mix combining cumin powder, coriander powder, turmeric powder, kashmiri red chilli powder, and gorom moshla.",
      "Finely chop ginger, green chillies, onions, and coriander leaves. Roughly chop garlic. Cut tomatoes into small cubes.",
      "Heat mustard oil in a kadai and add ghee. Add onions and fry until golden. This should take around 4 minutes. Now, add ginger, garlic, and green chillies consecutively. Fry each for 30 seconds.",
      "Add the spice mix and sauté on medium heat for another 4 minutes or so. In case the pan dries out, add a splash of water and continue frying.",
      "Lastly, add the cubed tomatoes and salt. Sauté the mixture until oil separates.",
      "Add the soaked and drained tadka'r and chhola'r daal to the pan. Sauté them with the spices on medium heat for 2 minutes. Then, pour 300 ml hot water.",
      "Transfer everything to a pressure cooker.",
      "Add mutton fat. Put the lid on and pressure-cook for 10 minutes.",
      "When you are ready to eat, heat a wok or pan on high flame. Once screaming hot, add vegetable oil. Add the onions, green chillies, garlic, and tomatoes. Toss everything on high heat.",
      "\\[If you feel comfortable doing it, tilt the pan towards the flame so that the ingredients 'catch fire' momentarily. This will give the tadka a smoky flavour. However, be very careful while doing this.\\]",
      "Ladle in a couple of portions of the boiled tadka and give everything a stir. Top with a generous amount of butter and let it melt.",
      "Garnish with chopped coriander leaves and crushed kasuri methi. Give everything one last mix and your plain tadka is ready!",
      "Beat two eggs with a pinch of salt. Add these to the tadka, allowing the eggs to set a bit before scrambling them.",
      "Stir gently and be careful not to cook too long, or the eggs will become dry and rubbery."
    ],
